# Web app configuration
# Copy to `apps/web/.env` for local development. Vite loads `.env` in every mode
# (plus `.env.local`, `.env.[mode]`, `.env.[mode].local`); only `VITE_`-prefixed
# variables reach the browser, and this file needs none. Hosting platforms supply
# the production values.

# Origin of the Express API this server forwards `/api/*` to — read by the server
# only, never the client bundle. An origin, not a base path: the API mounts its
# routers at the root. Leave unset locally to use the default
# (`http://localhost:8000`, where `pnpm --filter api dev` listens).
#
# In production, point it at a private address only this server can reach, then
# keep the API off the public internet. The API's `CORS_ORIGIN` still names the
# public web origin, which its state-changing routes check. A production server
# with no value answers `502` rather than guessing.
API_UPSTREAM_URL=http://localhost:8000